   "html_text": "Notwithstanding the computational interest of one-dimensional CA, philosophical issues have been discussed more often in connection with two-dimensional CA. The first CA, von Neumann’s self-reproducing automaton, inhabited a two-dimensional grid. Besides, two-dimensional CA are suitable for representing many physical, biological, and even human phenomena, ranging from the dynamics of perfect gases to the movements of birds in a storm and soldiers on a battlefield. The most common configurations ",
